    {
      "code": "CONFOUNDING",
      "text": "Changes in points per possession can be influenced by numerous factors besides offensive reorganization, such as the quality of the absent player, the quality of the replacement, opponent strength, game pace, and other simultaneous team adjustments. Isolating the effect of reorganization requires robust controls."
