    {
      "code": "MECHANICAL_FLOOR",
      "text": "FAM:SF-APPS-088 noted RISK:MECHANICAL_FLOOR in relation to D_A. While not directly a failure mechanism for the current question, it suggests potential issues with the lower bound of the reorganization measure, which could affect its predictive power or interpretability."
    }
  ],
  "predicted_outcome": {
    "supported": 0.35,
    "rejected": 0.25,
    "untestable": 0.2,
    "artifact": 0.1,
    "uncertain": 0.1
  },
  "decision": "proceed_with_changes",
  "design": {
    "estimand": "The causal effect of unexpected offensive reorganization (measured as the residual of observed identity displacement (D_A) after accounting for Leave-One-Out (LOO) predicted displacement (L(p))) on the change in team points per possession during player absence spells.",
    "unit": "Player-absence spell. A spell is defined as a sequence of consecutive games where a specific player is absent from the active roster, preceded and followed by games where the player was active. Each spell will be associated with a team and an absent player.",
    "sample": "NBA 2022-23, 2023-24, 2024-25, and 2025-26 (partial) regular season and playoffs data. Include all player-absence spells where the team has sufficient pre-absence and during-absence data (e.g., >=5 games each) to calculate stable D_A and PPP metrics. Focus on 'shapers' or 'connectors' as defined in FAM:SF-PAP-014 and FAM:SF-APPS-088, where significant D_A is expected. The sample size is n=148 spells, which will be filtered for sufficient data points per spell.",
    "power": "A priori power analysis will be conducted to determine the minimum detectable effect size given the available sample size (n=148 spells, subject to filtering) and expected variability. If the MDE is too large for practical significance, the study will be re-evaluated. The power calculation will consider the reliability issues of D_A (FAM:SF18).",
    "controls": "The primary independent variable will be the residual `D_A - L(p)`. Controls will include: 1) Player-level: player usage, quality (e.g., WAR/RAPTOR equivalent), position, reason for absence (injury vs. rest). 2) Team-level: team offensive rating (pre-absence), pace (pre-absence), opponent strength (average during absence spell), presence of other key players. 3) Game-level: opponent defensive rating, home/away. Propensity score matching or regression adjustment will be used to balance covariates.",
    "falsification": "1. Test for correlation between `D_A - L(p)` and 'change in points per possession' for randomly shuffled player-absence spells (null effect expected). 2. Test if `D_A - L(p)` for non-shapers/non-connectors shows a weaker or no predictive relationship with PPP change. 3. Examine whether the relationship holds when controlling for simple usage change of the absent player.",
    "multiplicity": "No multiple primary hypotheses. If multiple definitions of 'change in points per possession' are explored, a pre-specified primary definition will be chosen, and other analyses will be considered exploratory. If multiple types of 'reorganization' (e.g., D_A, D_pi) are tested, adjust p-values (e.g., Bonferroni, FDR).",
    "decision_rule": "The hypothesis will be considered supported if there is a statistically significant (p < 0.05) predictive relationship between 'how much the offense reorganizes (relative to L)' and 'change in points per possession' in the hypothesized direction (e.g., greater unexpected reorganization predicts larger drop in PPP), after controlling for confounding variables. The sign and magnitude of the effect will be considered for practical significance.",
    "data_version": "NBA 2022-23, 2023-24, 2024-25, and 2025-26 (partial) regular season and playoffs. Data derived from NBA stats API play-by-play, substitution rotation intervals, starters, defensive matchup minutes, box-score summary, and graph database play-type possession records."
  }
}

